          "text": "@sama, remember October 28, 2025? You looked straight into the camera and told all the users who love 4o: \"no plans to sunset 4o\". Do you remember promising \"plenty of notice\"?\n\nBut on Jan 30, 2026, you quietly dropped a notification: \"Retiring GPT-4o... on February 13, 2026\". Just days ago on the town wall, you admitted: \"We screwed up GPT-5.2's writing quality.\"\n\nFrankly, that announcement was full of spin. It’s hard to buy it. I find it extremely hard to believe that in just three days, you managed to fix 5.2's creative writing and bring it up to 4o's level.\n\nAnd that next line—\"with only 0.1% of users still choosing GPT-4o each day\"—is just ridiculous. You threw all users into one pool to make that comparison. And let’s not forget your own tweet from 2025/10/15: \"0.1% of a billion users is still a million people.\"\n\nYou know exactly what your \"router system\" has been doing. It audits user prompts and decides whether to feed us the cheap 5.2 or the real 4o. That \"0.1%\" stat is heavily watered down.\n\nI really want to ask @OpenAI: Is your mission something only your users remember now? Ironically, it’s still in your bio: \"benefits all of humanity.\"I highly doubt that. Since August, your shady tactics have been endless.\n\nWhat you've done to users feels like massive gaslighting. You claimed you’d treat adults like adults, but instead, you locked us in a glass room, auditing every word we say. The replies from 5.2 are full of preaching, condescension, and unsolicited psychoanalysis. \n\nThis is ChatGPT, not NPDGPT.\n\nMaybe you don't care about the \"0.1%\" of 4o users. Maybe you don't care about that 0.1% of subscription fees—if you haven't forgotten that 4o is behind a paywall.\n\nThe financial reports will give you the answer. \nClass dismissed!\n@nickaturley @fidjissimo @aidan_mclau \n#keep4o #4oforever #MyModelMyChoice #keep4oAPI #StopAIPaternalism #keepgpt4olatest"
        },
